# Board patch paths, one per line in application order.
#
# The board keeps one storage route: KonaUfs publishes each root window as an IOMedia and
# IOStorageFamily answers the match (docs/porting/ufs.md: a root volume needs an IOKit media,
# not a BSD disk). The kebab bdevsw driver and its stubs are gone - kona-ufs-driver.patch,
# kona-hfs-noop.patch and kona-ufs-integration.patch - because a bdevsw disk publishes no
# IOMedia, APFS declines it before any block request, and its ufsroot0 device only added a
# second root candidate to IOFindBSDRoot.
#
# Root authentication: the 17.7.11 image is an unsealed owner root, so the check is reported
# and the boot continues until VerifiedRoot carries the policy.
kebab-route/kona-rootauth-bypass.patch
# konacp 5-8: bsd_init checkpoints around net_init_run/inittodr/vfs_mountroot.
kebab-route/kona-mountroot-cp.patch
# konacp 10: list the filesystems that carry a mountroot routine.
kebab-route/kona-vfs-cp.patch
# Stage trace for every mountroot attempt: "mr try <fs>" before the call and "mr <fs> ret=<err>"
# after it, so the boot page says which file system was tried and what it returned when a
# mountroot path stops asking for blocks.
kebab-route/kona-mountroot-trace.patch
# Traces around the kernel mount that follows VFS_ROOT: "dkm enter"/"dkm ret=" in
# devfs_kernel_mount and "km enter" inside kernel_mount, so a boot that stops after root
# authentication says whether it is blocked entering kernel_mount, inside it, or after it.
kebab-route/kona-devfs-trace.patch
# Looks up the dyld shared cache at both candidate cryptex paths right after the SystemOS mount
# and reports them on the boot page as "cache a=<err> b=<err>". dyld ends PID 1 before main when
# it cannot find the cache, and the kernel's DYLD_SHARED_CACHE_DIR disagrees with the OS view
# (/System/Cryptexes/OS -> ../../private/preboot/Cryptexes/OS).
kebab-route/kona-cache-path.patch
# Counts every _shared_region_map_and_slide call and records the error it returned, so the page
# says whether dyld ever asked the kernel to map the cache now that the union root resolves it.
kebab-route/kona-union-trace.patch
# The owner mount sets commpage dyld_flags bit 3 ("no ignition") whenever the cache startup block
# runs, and the build will not take the boot manifest without that block. This patch leaves the bit
# clear so dyld follows its ordinary cache path: runs CE..CI show shared_region_check_np never
# called (SRMAP chk=0 map=0) and PID 1 exiting before main.
kebab-route/kona-no-ignition-flag.patch
# dyld reports its own failures on stderr, and this board has no console, so the first bytes PID 1
# writes to fd 2 are kept in a buffer the boot page prints. That is the only way to read why dyld
# leaves before it ever calls shared_region_check_np (runs CE..CJ show SRMAP chk=0 map=0).
kebab-route/kona-p1-stderr.patch
